  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Magnesium levulinate and Selenoprotein P, mediated through Selgantolimod. Multiple paths indicate that Magnesium levulinate targets three different entities—Keratin, type II cytoskeletal 6A, Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A, and Plasma kallikrein—all of which are targets of Selgantolimod. Selgantolimod, in turn, is known to target Selenoprotein P. The high scores across these paths (final_score=0.7073) suggest a consistent and significant relationship, likely due to the shared involvement of Selgantolimod as a bridge between Magnesium levulinate and Selenoprotein P. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway where Magnesium levulinate may influence the activity or expression of these intermediate targets, which are subsequently targeted by Selgantolimod to reach Selenoprotein P. The findings imply that Magnesium levulinate could modulate Selenoprotein P through this indirect route, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
